1
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:27,775
Deep underground, in a small dark bedroom, red emergency
lights flicker. Eight-year-old Mia sleeps beneath an old
blanket. On the nightstand beside her rests a framed
photograph... of Mia and her mother.

2
00:00:28,625 --> 00:00:36,483
ECHO-07 stands beside her bed, watching her quietly. Inside
him, red warnings flash.

3
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,909
Mia slowly opens her eyes.

4
00:00:40,259 --> 00:00:41,299
Mia: Echo?

5
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:42,628
Echo: Yes, Mia?

6
00:00:42,728 --> 00:00:45,040
Mia: Is Mommy coming home tomorrow?

7
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:53,359
A new warning flashes inside him. Echo looks toward the
photograph on the nightstand... and pauses.

8
00:00:53,709 --> 00:00:56,277
Echo: Yes, Mia. Tomorrow.

9
00:00:57,127 --> 00:01:00,248
Mia smiles, and closes her eyes.

10
00:01:00,598 --> 00:01:02,078
Mia: Goodnight, Echo.

11
00:01:02,178 --> 00:01:03,327
Echo: Goodnight, Mia.

12
00:01:04,177 --> 00:01:08,268
And Echo's cyan eyes dim... with sadness.

13
00:01:13,668 --> 00:01:29,000
Morning in the underground shelter. Echo stands at a small
kitchen counter as smoke rises from the toaster. At the
table, Mia watches... suspiciously. Echo proudly places a
plate of burnt black toast in front of her.

14
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:32,067
Mia: You burned it again.

15
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:35,886
Echo: Incorrect. It is eighty-seven percent toasted.

16
00:01:35,986 --> 00:01:38,207
Mia: It's BLACK!

17
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:40,810
Echo: A desirable shade of toast.

18
00:01:41,160 --> 00:01:46,552
Mia bursts into laughter, while Echo examines the toast,
looking confused.

19
00:01:46,902 --> 00:01:49,158
Echo: Would you prefer eighty-six percent?

20
00:01:49,258 --> 00:01:51,823
Mia: I'd prefer bread.

21
00:01:52,673 --> 00:02:01,092
Echo tilts his head. Later, they play chess. When Echo looks
away... Mia secretly moves one of his pieces.

22
00:02:01,442 --> 00:02:02,867
Echo: You are cheating.

23
00:02:02,967 --> 00:02:04,241
Mia: Prove it.

24
00:02:05,091 --> 00:02:13,566
Echo looks directly at the moved piece, his eyes
narrowing... then he deliberately moves another piece,
letting Mia win.

25
00:02:13,916 --> 00:02:15,155
Mia: Checkmate!

26
00:02:15,255 --> 00:02:17,230
Echo: An unexpected defeat.

27
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:29,834
Mia celebrates, and Echo's eyes curve into a smile.
Afterward, Mia draws a crayon picture of herself, Echo, and
her mother, holding hands beneath a bright sun.

28
00:02:30,184 --> 00:02:33,273
Mia: When Mommy comes back, we'll all go outside together.

29
00:02:33,373 --> 00:02:35,552
Echo: That sounds... wonderful.

30
00:02:36,402 --> 00:02:39,212
Mia tapes the drawing to Echo's chest.

31
00:02:39,562 --> 00:02:41,377
Mia: Now we're a family.

32
00:02:42,227 --> 00:02:49,977
Echo looks down at the drawing. His battery drops to ten
percent... and he quietly covers the warning with his hand.

33
00:02:55,377 --> 00:03:06,950
While Echo repairs equipment elsewhere, Mia explores a dim
corridor with her flashlight. The beam reveals a large,
locked metal door. Surface Access.

34
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,853
Mia: What's behind here?

35
00:03:09,703 --> 00:03:17,343
She touches the access panel. A red lock appears... and an
alarm sounds. Echo rushes into the corridor.

36
00:03:17,693 --> 00:03:19,997
Echo: Mia! Step away from the door.

37
00:03:20,097 --> 00:03:21,995
Mia: Why can't we go outside?

38
00:03:22,095 --> 00:03:23,943
Echo: The surface is unsafe.

39
00:03:24,793 --> 00:03:27,660
Mia looks at the door, then back at Echo.

40
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:32,446
Mia: But Mommy went outside. How many days has she been
gone?

41
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:35,685
Echo becomes completely still.

42
00:03:36,035 --> 00:03:37,789
Echo: You should return to your room.

43
00:03:38,389 --> 00:03:40,198
Mia: Echo. How many?

44
00:03:40,798 --> 00:03:42,146
Echo: I do not remember.

45
00:03:42,746 --> 00:03:44,948
Mia: But you remember everything.

46
00:03:45,798 --> 00:03:51,246
Disappointed, Mia walks away... leaving Echo alone beside
the door.

47
00:03:56,646 --> 00:04:01,124
That night, Mia wakes up... and Echo is gone.

48
00:04:01,474 --> 00:04:02,441
Mia: Echo?

49
00:04:03,291 --> 00:04:13,784
She follows a faint mechanical sound into a dark maintenance
room. Echo is kneeling beside a damaged charging station.
Sparks fly from the cables.

50
00:04:14,134 --> 00:04:17,917
Echo: Attempt twenty-seven... unsuccessful.

51
00:04:18,767 --> 00:04:31,124
Nearby, Mia notices an old computer terminal. On its
screen... her mother's photograph. She presses play. Doctor
Elena appears, in a flickering blue recording.

52
00:04:31,974 --> 00:04:44,500
Dr. Elena: Echo. If you're watching this, the evacuation has
failed. Keep Mia safe. She's only three. She won't
understand what's happening. If I don't return... promise me
you won't let her lose hope.

53
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,690
Echo: I promise.

54
00:04:46,540 --> 00:04:53,500
The recording ends. Startled, Mia knocks a metal container
to the floor. Echo turns around.

55
00:04:53,850 --> 00:04:59,148
Mia: I was three? You've been telling me tomorrow for FIVE
years?

56
00:04:59,248 --> 00:05:01,564
Echo: Mia, I was trying to...

57
00:05:01,664 --> 00:05:03,976
Mia: You lied to me!

58
00:05:04,826 --> 00:05:11,296
Mia runs out of the room. Echo stays beside the broken
charger... as his eyes dim.

59
00:05:16,696 --> 00:05:24,951
Mia sits alone on her bed, hugging her red scarf. Echo
approaches the closed door, carrying a small dinner tray.

60
00:05:25,801 --> 00:05:30,519
Echo: Mia. Your dinner is ready. I did not burn the toast.

61
00:05:31,119 --> 00:05:33,478
Mia: Go away.

62
00:05:34,328 --> 00:05:38,582
Echo slowly lowers the tray, and sits down against the
closed door.

63
00:05:39,432 --> 00:05:41,719
Mia: You said robots can't lie.

64
00:05:42,319 --> 00:05:43,808
Echo: We are not supposed to.

65
00:05:44,408 --> 00:05:46,012
Mia: Then why did you?

66
00:05:46,862 --> 00:05:48,443
Echo looks at the floor.

67
00:05:48,793 --> 00:05:55,432
Echo: The first time I told you she would return... you
stopped crying. I wanted you to smile again.

68
00:05:56,282 --> 00:05:59,922
Inside the bedroom, Mia looks at her mother's photograph.

69
00:06:00,272 --> 00:06:02,202
Mia: That doesn't make it okay.

70
00:06:02,802 --> 00:06:04,775
Echo: No. It does not.

71
00:06:05,375 --> 00:06:07,830
Mia: I hate you.

72
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,403
Echo: Understood.

73
00:06:10,253 --> 00:06:18,189
He leaves the tray outside her door. Suddenly... the lights
flicker. Echo looks toward the forbidden surface door.

74
00:06:23,589 --> 00:06:31,938
The whole shelter loses power. Darkness... then the red
emergency lights kick on. Mia wakes up, frightened.

75
00:06:32,288 --> 00:06:33,306
Mia: Echo?

76
00:06:34,156 --> 00:06:37,463
Echo enters, holding her bright yellow raincoat.

77
00:06:37,813 --> 00:06:39,119
Echo: We have to leave.

78
00:06:39,219 --> 00:06:41,390
Mia: Leave? Where?

79
00:06:41,490 --> 00:06:42,525
Echo: Outside.

80
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:54,773
At the Surface Access door, Echo enters an emergency
override code. The heavy door slowly grinds open... and warm
golden sunlight floods the dark corridor.

81
00:06:55,623 --> 00:07:08,875
Mia and Echo step out into a breathtaking, abandoned city...
overgrown with green vines, blooming flowers and clear
flowing streams. Birds soar across the bright sky.

82
00:07:09,725 --> 00:07:12,912
Mia: Wow... You said it wasn't safe.

83
00:07:13,012 --> 00:07:15,946
Echo: The last surface readings were five years old.

84
00:07:16,046 --> 00:07:17,628
Mia: You could've checked.

85
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:18,563
Echo: Yes.

86
00:07:19,413 --> 00:07:24,605
A colorful butterfly flutters down, and lands on Mia's
outstretched hand.

87
00:07:24,955 --> 00:07:27,123
Mia: I've never seen a real one.

88
00:07:27,973 --> 00:07:31,297
Suddenly, Echo's sensors pick up a faint signal.

89
00:07:31,647 --> 00:07:34,442
Echo: Mia. There are other people.

90
00:07:34,542 --> 00:07:35,513
Mia: Mommy?

91
00:07:35,613 --> 00:07:36,656
Echo: I don't know.

92
00:07:37,506 --> 00:07:40,880
Mia looks toward the distant radio tower on the horizon.

93
00:07:41,230 --> 00:07:42,796
Mia: Then let's find out.

94
00:07:48,196 --> 00:07:56,461
As they walk through the overgrown streets, Mia picks a
small wildflower, and tucks it beside the crayon drawing on
Echo's chest.

95
00:07:56,811 --> 00:07:58,646
Mia: Now you look official.

96
00:07:58,746 --> 00:08:00,589
Echo: I was already official.

97
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:11,166
Mia smiles. By sunset, they reach an old ruined bridge
leading toward the radio tower, its red beacon flashing in
the distance.

98
00:08:12,016 --> 00:08:20,094
Echo's steps grow slower. His damaged arm twitches... until
his knees give way, and he collapses onto the bridge.

99
00:08:20,444 --> 00:08:21,471
Mia: Echo!

100
00:08:22,321 --> 00:08:25,365
She kneels beside him as he struggles to get up.

101
00:08:25,715 --> 00:08:28,538
Echo: A temporary malfunction.

102
00:08:28,888 --> 00:08:31,816
Mia sees the flashing light on his chest.

103
00:08:32,166 --> 00:08:34,526
Mia: Stop lying!

104
00:08:34,626 --> 00:08:36,375
Echo: My battery is depleted.

105
00:08:36,475 --> 00:08:38,344
Mia: Then we'll find another one.

106
00:08:38,444 --> 00:08:42,494
Echo: There is insufficient time. You must continue without
me.

107
00:08:43,344 --> 00:08:45,662
Mia shakes her head, firmly.

108
00:08:46,012 --> 00:08:46,936
Mia: No.

109
00:08:47,036 --> 00:08:47,837
Echo: Mia...

110
00:08:47,937 --> 00:08:49,640
Mia: You're my family too.

111
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:55,088
Mia holds out her hand. A soft smile appears in Echo's eyes.

112
00:08:55,438 --> 00:08:57,797
Echo: Then we will go together.

113
00:08:58,647 --> 00:09:06,033
With her red scarf blowing in the sunset wind, Mia supports
Echo's weight... as they cross the bridge together.

114
00:09:11,433 --> 00:09:20,894
Night falls as they reach the abandoned radio station. Echo
examines the emergency transmitter, pressing switches... but
nothing turns on.

115
00:09:21,244 --> 00:09:23,493
Echo: The transmitter has no power.

116
00:09:24,343 --> 00:09:31,050
Echo looks at the loose power cables... then down at his own
chest. He picks up a heavy cable.

117
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,280
Mia: What are you doing?

118
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:36,900
Echo plugs the cable directly into his chest.

119
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:40,184
Echo: Mia. I need you to press that button.

120
00:09:40,534 --> 00:09:41,952
She hesitates.

121
00:09:42,302 --> 00:09:43,273
Echo: Please.

122
00:09:44,123 --> 00:09:53,176
Mia presses the button. Blue lights glow across the console.
Static crackles from the speaker... and then, a voice.

123
00:09:53,526 --> 00:09:56,438
Radio: Hello? Is somebody there?

124
00:09:57,288 --> 00:09:59,069
Mia grabs the microphone.

125
00:09:59,419 --> 00:10:02,372
Mia: Please help! My friend is dying!

126
00:10:02,472 --> 00:10:04,652
Radio: Stay where you are. We're coming.

127
00:10:05,502 --> 00:10:07,180
Mia turns to Echo.

128
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:11,143
Mia: They're coming! You heard them! They'll fix you.

129
00:10:11,493 --> 00:10:15,414
Echo's eyes begin to flicker. Mia takes his hand.

130
00:10:15,764 --> 00:10:17,621
Mia: Promise me you'll be okay.

131
00:10:18,471 --> 00:10:22,284
Echo looks down at the crayon family drawing on his chest.

132
00:10:22,634 --> 00:10:23,826
Echo: I promise.

133
00:10:24,676 --> 00:10:30,119
Echo's cyan eyes slowly dim to black. His hand goes still.

134
00:10:30,469 --> 00:10:33,140
Mia: Echo? Echo!

135
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:41,143
Mia wraps her arms around him... as the headlights of a
distant rescue vehicle shine through the station windows.

136
00:10:46,543 --> 00:10:54,046
Three weeks later, morning sunlight fills a peaceful
settlement, surrounded by gardens and rebuilt homes.

137
00:10:54,896 --> 00:11:02,446
Inside a warm wooden workshop, Mia waits anxiously beside
Echo, as a technician connects a new power cell.

138
00:11:02,796 --> 00:11:04,455
Technician: Let's see if this works.

139
00:11:05,305 --> 00:11:10,043
Echo's systems hum to life. His cyan eyes light up.

140
00:11:10,393 --> 00:11:11,454
Mia: Echo!

141
00:11:11,554 --> 00:11:15,622
Echo: Hello. I am ECHO-07. How may I assist you?

142
00:11:16,472 --> 00:11:24,505
Mia's smile fades. Slowly, she takes out their worn crayon
drawing, and places it into Echo's hands.

143
00:11:24,855 --> 00:11:27,439
Mia: It's okay. We can start again.

144
00:11:28,289 --> 00:11:34,828
She turns toward the door. Behind her, Echo looks down at
the drawing... his eyes flickering.

145
00:11:35,178 --> 00:11:35,904
Echo: Mia?

146
00:11:36,254 --> 00:11:39,731
She freezes... and slowly turns around.

147
00:11:40,081 --> 00:11:42,119
Mia: You remember me?

148
00:11:42,719 --> 00:11:46,493
Echo: I remember... that you prefer your toast unburned.

149
00:11:47,343 --> 00:12:00,675
Laughing through her tears, Mia runs to him and throws her
arms around him. Echo gently holds her close, their family
drawing in his hand... as warm morning sunlight fills the
workshop.

150
00:12:01,025 --> 00:12:02,013
The End.
